WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.701
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.968
You're here.
You're watching at home.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:06.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you very much.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:10.734
We're very excited here, guys.
Christmas is only 11 days away.

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:13.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.501
Yeah, last week, you went,
"How much for shipping?"

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.734
And now it's like,
"$59.99 and my first born?

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:20.300
Let's do this. Okay."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.667
Get this --I saw a new survey

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:24.267
that said New Yorkers'
least-favorite Christmas food

00:00:24.267 --> 00:00:26.334
is peppermint bark.

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:27.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.834 --> 00:00:29.434
I like peppermint bark.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.934
[ Laughter ]
I do.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.901
I especially like
how the chocolate soothes

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:36.133
the open wounds caused
by the shards of candy cane.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.634
[Gravelly voice]
"Merry Christmas."

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:40.267
[Normal voice]
The survey also found

00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:42.467
the most popular
Christmas food is...

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.067
-Ritz crackers.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:46.033
-Ritz crackers? No.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:48.601
That's not Christmas food.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:51.968
Ritz crackers?
I mean, it's a food, sure.

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.234
It's like...

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:54.834
Pigs in a blanket.

00:00:54.834 --> 00:00:56.701
[ Audience oohs ]

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:59.033
Jesus was like, "Thanks for
keeping my birthday classy.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.367
Appreciate it."

00:01:00.367 --> 00:01:01.667
Pigs in a blanket.

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:03.234
Apparently on Christmas,
people ask themselves,

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:06.834
"What would Jesus'
brother-in-law Randy do?"

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:08.667
I read that right now --
I love --

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:10.634
By the way,
I love pigs in a blanket.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.734
-I'm all for it.
-I'm all for it, man.

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:14.868
I read that right now
the cost of ingredients

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:17.968
for popular holiday desserts
is surging.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.100
Thankfully, every family
has that same blue tin

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.434
of Danish butter cookies

00:01:21.434 --> 00:01:23.367
that's been floating around
for 20 years.

00:01:23.367 --> 00:01:25.567
"We didn't finish these yet?

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:27.434
How come no one's eating
these square ones

00:01:27.434 --> 00:01:30.000
with no sugar on them?"

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.667
Listen to this.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:35.634
According to a poll,
one-third of Americans

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:39.267
start buying holiday gifts
two months in advance.

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:41.534
That's risky 'cause a lot
can happen in two months.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.367
It's like, "Here's that Kanye
sweatshirt you wanted."

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:45.801
You go, "Hey. Wait. Hold on."

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:47.400
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:49.167
"Put it in the box."

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:53.267
♪♪

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:55.167
Speaking of presents,
this year,

00:01:55.167 --> 00:01:59.000
75% of people said they plan to
buy gifts from small businesses.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.667
Yeah.

00:02:02.667 --> 00:02:03.834
Small businesses.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:05.300
When they heard that,
Santa's elves were like,

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.167
"One more short joke,
and I'm gonna cut somebody!"

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:11.234
And you go, "No, no.
It's not a shor--

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.767
Small businesses."

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.501
75% of people want to shop
at small businesses,

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.267
which explains this ad I saw.
-Oh, really?

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:20.501
-This holiday season, support
your local mom-and-pop shop --

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:21.734
Amazon!

00:02:21.734 --> 00:02:23.067
We know what you're thinking.

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:26.501
How does a "family business"
have 800,000 employees?

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:29.067
Easy. We're all cousins.

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:31.801
That's not a warehouse.
That's a family reunion.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.901
Get back to work, family.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:37.167
Amazon. Help! We're tiny!

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.501
-Yeah. Aww. Mom-and-pop.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:42.601
[ Applause ]

00:02:42.601 --> 00:02:44.767
Well, let's get to some news.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:47.400
President Biden has reportedly
vented to allies

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.734
over how much the media
talks about his age.

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:51.300
And at one point he even said,

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.634
"You think I don't know
how F'ing old I am?"

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:56.634
[ Laughter ]
This is a real thing. Yeah.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.667
His staff was like,
"Of course you do,

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:01.033
but just to be safe,
toss out a number."

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:02.801
[ Laughter ]
"Higher."

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:05.567
Yeah. Biden was furious.

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.501
It only got worse
when his chief of staff said,

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:10.534
"Well, he hasn't had
his nap today, so..."

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:12.400
Biden was upset. He cursed.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:14.167
He ran up to his bedroom,
slammed the door,

00:03:14.167 --> 00:03:15.400
cranked up Bing Crosby.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.834
"You don't know me!"

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:19.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:21.667
Some more political news.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.567
Since announcing his 2024 run,

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:26.534
former President Trump
has been relatively quiet,

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:29.334
but today he said that he's
planning a major announcement

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.901
and posted this video.
This is real.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:33.367
We didn't make this.
Take a look.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.534
[ Dramatic music swells ]

00:03:37.534 --> 00:03:39.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:43.701
♪♪

00:03:43.701 --> 00:03:45.934
-Jimmy:
"Major announcement."

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:47.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:48.767
"Major..."
-God.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.868
-Is he announcing Dean Cain
as his running mate?

00:03:50.868 --> 00:03:52.067
I don't know what he's --

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.667
I think the major announcement
is that Trump

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:56.167
has a lot of time on his hands.
Okay.

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:57.567
Right after that was released,

00:03:57.567 --> 00:04:00.701
Ron DeSantis' poll numbers
shot up another 20 points.

00:04:00.701 --> 00:04:02.634
Can we see that picture again?

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:04.100
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my goodness.

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.300
Let's be real.
If Trump tore his shirt open,

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.567
we'd probably see
five layers of Spanx.

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:09.968
You know?

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:12.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.567
Come on.

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:16.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:16.734 --> 00:04:20.234
Switching gears, apparently
the IRS has been contacting

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:24.067
OnlyFans creators as part
of a criminal tax investigation.

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:25.567
-Ooh.

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:28.067
The IRS actually said they're
sending two agents at a time --

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.501
one to do the investigation

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:31.200
and the other to make sure
that the first guy

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.801
is actually doing
the investigation.

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:36.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.634
Get this.
Mark Zuckerberg is spending

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:40.868
so much time and money
on the Metaverse

00:04:40.868 --> 00:04:42.133
that employees are worried

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.000
that he's going to
destroy the company.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.067
Well, here to clear things up,
live, via satellite,

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:48.033
is Mark Zuckerberg. Mark?

00:04:48.033 --> 00:04:49.300
-Hey, Jimmy. Don't mind me.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:50.801
Just gonna be chilling
in the Metaverse

00:04:50.801 --> 00:04:52.133
while we do this interview.

00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:53.667
-Okay, sure.

00:04:53.667 --> 00:04:56.100
Mark, these are pretty serious
allegations from your employees.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:57.467
How do you respond to them?

00:04:57.467 --> 00:04:59.400
-What you're hearing in
the press is really overblown.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.133
We're investing a lot
in the Metaverse, sure,

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.868
but don't worry.
I'm giving it my full attention.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:06.467
[ Club whacks ball ]
Ugh! Sliced it!

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:08.300
-But your -- But your company

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.968
lost $80 billion worth
of stock value.

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.968
Do you have any ideas
on how to fix this?

00:05:12.968 --> 00:05:15.300
-Trust me, Jimmy. $80 billion
is a drop in the bucket.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.133
We'll gain it all right back.

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.901
Cinnamon! Cinnamon, notice me!

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:22.667
Notice me! Cinnamon!

00:05:22.667 --> 00:05:24.901
-"Cinnamon, notice..."
-What?!

00:05:24.901 --> 00:05:26.767
-I think that's
all the time we have.

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:28.934
Mark Zuckerberg, everybody.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:30.534
-Okay. Take care, Jimmy.
-Alright...

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:32.100
Alright.

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:36.801
Guys, I heard
that the CEO of Taco Bell says

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:39.968
gen Z wants to eat chicken
instead of beef.

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:41.567
[ Cheers ]

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:43.033
Then they added,
"But it doesn't affect us

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:45.367
'cause what we serve
is technically neither."

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:47.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.567 --> 00:05:49.534
You're all clear.

00:05:49.534 --> 00:05:52.467
Don't worry about it.
Whatever you want. It's both.

00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:55.000
That's how I remember.
I had the lasagna. Yeah.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.300
Some more business news.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.334
Costco is planning
to raise the price

00:05:58.334 --> 00:05:59.567
of their annual membership.

00:05:59.567 --> 00:06:01.501
-Ooh.
-[ Audience boos ]

00:06:01.501 --> 00:06:03.133
-Yeah, Costco is
getting more expensive,

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:04.968
and you can tell
they're a little fancier now.

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:06.167
Watch this ad I saw.

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:08.601
-Welcome to ze new Costco.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.801
Ze home of elegance.

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:13.934
A seven-pound bucket of Nutella.

00:06:13.934 --> 00:06:15.667
Sophistication.

00:06:15.667 --> 00:06:19.000
Turtlenecks and batteries
on the same aisle.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.434
And class.

00:06:20.434 --> 00:06:23.367
Old people eating hot dogs.

00:06:23.367 --> 00:06:26.701
Costco. Like Walmart
with a doorman.

00:06:26.701 --> 00:06:28.300
-That's...

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.067
That's interesting, I thought.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:31.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:31.801 --> 00:06:34.400
-"Costco."

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.868
-You guys --
Have you guys seen this?

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:37.868
The newest trend being
brought back in style

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:39.968
is the lower-back tattoo.

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:41.634
[ Audience groans ]

00:06:41.634 --> 00:06:44.033
As we speak, a bunch
of 40-year-old guys are like,

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:47.901
"Maybe a calf tattoo of Calvin
peeing isn't far behind?"

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:50.167
Yep, lower-back tattoos
are back.

00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:52.567
Well, now I think we know what
Trump's big announcement is.

00:06:52.567 --> 00:06:55.300
Yeah.
"Check out my Trump stamp."

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.100
[ Applause ]

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:01.000
Finally, we have
exactly three shows left

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.567
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time

00:07:03.567 --> 00:07:05.434
for that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:07:05.434 --> 00:07:07.367
It's time for "12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters."

00:07:07.367 --> 00:07:09.000
Here we go.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.400
-♪ 12 days of
Christmas sweaters ♪

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:15.801
♪ Three days left ♪

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:19.467
-That's right. Every show
between now and Christmas,

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:22.000
we'll be giving
one lucky audience member

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.534
a bodacious Christmas sweater

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:26.534
from the
Countdown to Christmas Cabinet.

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:29.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's right!

00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:33.534
And since -- since
there are three shows left,

00:07:33.534 --> 00:07:36.067
let's open door number 3.

00:07:36.067 --> 00:07:39.534
[ Drum roll ]

00:07:39.534 --> 00:07:41.367
-Ooh!
-Ooh!

00:07:41.367 --> 00:07:45.968
♪♪

00:07:45.968 --> 00:07:48.434
-Wow. Thank you very much.

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:49.834
-Yes. Of course.

00:07:49.834 --> 00:07:53.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:53.267 --> 00:07:55.334
[ Laughter ]

00:07:55.334 --> 00:07:58.334
-Wow. Can we dim the lights
a little bit?

00:07:58.334 --> 00:08:00.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:04.868 --> 00:08:07.267
Hm. Beautiful. Alright.

00:08:07.267 --> 00:08:09.767
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:08:09.767 --> 00:08:11.467
Everyone look
at your seat number.

00:08:11.467 --> 00:08:13.234
If I call your number,
come on down.

00:08:13.234 --> 00:08:15.400
Quest, can I get
a drum roll, please?

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:18.934
[ Drum roll ]

00:08:18.934 --> 00:08:21.000
3-0-2!

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:24.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:24.534 --> 00:08:27.033
Come on down! Hey!

00:08:27.033 --> 00:08:29.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:36.067
♪♪

00:08:36.067 --> 00:08:42.767
♪♪

00:08:42.767 --> 00:08:46.534
Hello! Ha!

00:08:46.534 --> 00:08:47.968
Hello. How you doing?

00:08:47.968 --> 00:08:50.567
Nice to see you.
What is your name?

00:08:50.567 --> 00:08:52.100
-Jackie.
-Jackie, where are you from?

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:53.601
-Long Island.
-Long Island!

00:08:53.601 --> 00:08:56.834
I love Long Island!
I love Long Island.

00:08:56.834 --> 00:08:59.133
I know it gets a little chilly
out on Long Island.

00:08:59.133 --> 00:09:00.601
You'll have a beautiful sweater.

00:09:00.601 --> 00:09:01.968
-Thank you.
-But it's missing --

00:09:01.968 --> 00:09:04.367
It has a couple
of beautiful holes in it.

00:09:04.367 --> 00:09:06.133
I think you'll need this
in Long Island.

00:09:06.133 --> 00:09:08.634
And you'll just fit right in.
No one will even know
you're wearing it.

00:09:08.634 --> 00:09:10.300
-No one will even know.
-Would you like to try it on
right now for everybody?

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.100
-Absolutely.
-Oh, this is going to be fun.

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:14.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:15.767
Here you go.

00:09:15.767 --> 00:09:19.000
There's no right way to put it
on. I gotta be honest.

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.467
Well, you've got your arms
in the sleeve. That's a win.

00:09:21.467 --> 00:09:24.033
♪♪

00:09:24.033 --> 00:09:25.100
Ohh!

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.167
Oh, my gosh. Look at you.

00:09:30.167 --> 00:09:32.901
Look at this. You look gorgeous.

00:09:32.901 --> 00:09:34.067
Look.

00:09:34.067 --> 00:09:36.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:40.167
You look beautiful! Oh, my gosh.
Is that not fantastic?

00:09:40.167 --> 00:09:41.767
Happy holidays.
Nice to see you.

00:09:41.767 --> 00:09:44.033
Thank you for coming
to the show. You look great.

00:09:44.033 --> 00:09:45.567
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:09:45.567 --> 00:09:47.267
You can go up to your seat.
Thank you very much.

00:09:47.267 --> 00:09:48.934
-Thank you so much.

00:09:48.934 --> 00:09:51.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:51.167 --> 00:09:52.834
That's the best.

00:09:52.834 --> 00:09:55.133
♪♪

00:09:55.133 --> 00:09:57.501
Can we get a camera shot
of her going --

00:09:57.501 --> 00:10:01.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:01.033 --> 00:10:04.334
Oh, my God.

00:10:04.334 --> 00:10:06.567
You don't even know
it's happening.

00:10:06.567 --> 00:10:08.968
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.968 --> 00:10:10.534
Oh, you look great.

00:10:10.534 --> 00:10:12.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:12.834 --> 00:10:15.100
Well done.
-Whoo!

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.534
You know what?

00:10:17.534 --> 00:10:20.400
You know what?
I'm in the giving spirit. I am.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
I really am.

00:10:22.167 --> 00:10:24.334
Why does just one person
get a gift?

00:10:24.334 --> 00:10:27.033
Why can't everyone
in the audience get a gift?

00:10:27.033 --> 00:10:29.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's right!

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.801
It's time for "Tonight Show"
Stocking Stuffers!

00:10:31.801 --> 00:10:33.200
Here we go!

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.567
-♪ "Tonight Show" ♪
-♪ Stocking Stuffers ♪

00:10:35.567 --> 00:10:37.667
♪ It's the "Tonight Show" ♪
-♪ Stocking Stuffers ♪

00:10:37.734 --> 00:10:41.400
-♪ Stocking Stuffers ♪

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:42.901 --> 00:10:45.200
-Every night
until Christmas break,

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.934
